  "solution": "**Concept Used:**\n\n**First term × 2 + 4 = Second term**\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nLet's apply the pattern on the given pairs:\n\n1) 0 : 6\n\n __**0 × 2**__ + 4 = 6\n\n __**0 + 4**__ = 6 \n\n 4 ≠ 6 \n\n2) 12 : 28\n\n __12 × 2__ + 4 = 28\n __**24**____ + 4__ = 28 \n 28 = 28\n\n3) 21 : 46\n __21 × 2__ + 4 = 46\n __**42**____ + 4__ = 46\n 46 = 46\n\n2) 5 : 14\n __5 × 2__ + 4 = 14\n __10____ + 4__ = 14 \n 14 = 14\n\nSo, **0:6 is the odd one.**\n\nHence **the correct answer is option 1)**",
